+# Empty reflection path: issue #1144
+
+The proposed `TestEmptyReflectionPath` regression uses one building, one point
+source on its wall, and one receiver. Its `main` method also runs as a standalone
+witness against the unmodified 5.0.1 no-GUI release. The current release throws
+`IndexOutOfBoundsException` at `PathFinder.java:761`.
+
+The intended handling of the geometry needs confirmation in
+[issue #1144](https://github.com/Universite-Gustave-Eiffel/NoiseModelling/issues/1144).
+The source-on-wall condition is also covered by the proposal in
+[PR #1005](https://github.com/Universite-Gustave-Eiffel/NoiseModelling/pull/1005).
+The regression is a draft witness; the expected acoustic result or validated
+error should be agreed before finalizing its assertion. Production code is
+unchanged.
+
+For the original three H2 inputs, use an existing checkout of the
+[public reproduction bundle](https://github.com/rdmitry0911/noisemodelling-5.0.1-computeReflexion-repro)
+and run the optional manual script:
+
+```sh
+python3 noisemodelling-pathfinder/src/test/scripts/repro_issue_1144.py \
+  --stock /path/to/NoiseModelling_without_gui-5.0.1 \
+  --java-home /path/to/jdk17 \
+  --bundle /path/to/noisemodelling-5.0.1-computeReflexion-repro \
+  --out /path/to/new-output-directory
+```
+
+The script checks the three pristine SHA-256 values and the orchestration script
+before opening H2. It creates a new working copy per case, records the native exit
+code and trace, and verifies that the pristine sources remain unchanged. Its exit
+status is nonzero when a native run fails. All three inputs currently fail on
+5.0.1; a completed CSV is recorded separately. The databases remain in the bundle
+repository, with their original licensing status. This manual integration check
+adds no CI job or automatic download. The small Java witness needs no database.
